            <ArticleTitle>'Oblongata' crises in tabes dorsalis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1240-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient in the pre-ataxic stage of tabes dorsalis suffered from gastric crises, but in addition had numerous episodes of apnoea and coma which in the older literature have been described as 'oblongata crises'--the presumption being that the crises are due to a brain stem disturbance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
